<title>AUSTRALIA: Australia's AWB sells no wheat in tender 22.</title>
<headline>Australia's AWB sells no wheat in tender 22.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Australian Wheat Board (AWB) sold no wheat in the latest tender for the domestic sale of wheat from its national pool, AWB said in a statement.</p>
<p>Total bids were received for 20,000 tonnes of current crop wheat and for 6,000 tonnes of 1997/98 season wheat, it said.</p>
<p>The frequency of tenders was currently under review, it said.</p>
<p>Highest failed bids A$/tonne:</p>
<p>    Port zone   Grade   Current crop   New crop</p>
<p>    Newcastle   ASW     191.00	   181.50</p>
<p>    Port Kembla ASW     189.00</p>
<p>    Port Kembla Feed    182.00</p>
<p>    Geelong     ASW     192.00</p>
<p>    Geelong     Feed    172.00</p>
<p>The next tender would be held on May 14, AWB said.</p>
<p>Note: ASW = Australian Standard White</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
